    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "But the loop had a dark side. In the nineteen seventies, Western banks were overflowing with petrodollars, and they lent them out, much of it to Latin America. Then, starting in nineteen seventy nine, the U.S. Federal Reserve pushed interest rates sharply higher to crush inflation. At one point they hit around twenty percent. Loans in dollars suddenly became crushing. In August nineteen eighty two, Mexico announced it could no longer pay. Country after country followed, and Latin America fell into what became known as the lost decade.",
